Subject: [PATCH 1/2] The classroom: Aria as a whole teacher who walks to the
 board and writes with a marker

A laptop demo at /classroom (LessonPlayer `classroom`). The board stays exactly as it is, full
height on a lit classroom wall in a light frame; Aria stands in front of it as a full-body
teacher, rendered on the student's own GPU at no cost per minute.

- The teacher: Microsoft Rocketbox Female_Adult_14 (MIT) with 14 motion-captured clips (talking
  gestures, presenting, listening, walking, crouching), its 15 viseme and 52 ARKit face shapes,
  converted to one 5 MB GLB. Her mouth takes the same viseme stream as the bust.
- The brain (lib/classroom/teacherBrain.ts, pure, tested): she explains from her own lane right of
  the board, half-turned to it and pointing now and then; comes to the middle to introduce a part;
  walks to the board when it writes, at her walk clip's own speed so her feet do not slide.
- Writing: the board's pen reports where its tip is; her left hand (left-handed on purpose, so
  she never stands on ink she has just written) holds a marker whose nib follows it through a
  two-bone IK arm and a real grip. She crouches for low lines. The pen waits for her while she
  walks or turns, as a real teacher's writing does; the board's floating pen icon hides while she
  is there.

scripts/avatar/classroom-tour.mjs walks the demo on the GPU and logs what she does each second.
docs/research/full-body-teacher-2026-10-09.md is the research report behind it.

